    "created_at": "2025-02-04T16:34:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-04T16:35:14Z",
    "body": "I doubt we really need `menu, dir` in the style fwiw, the websites that looked better in Firefox also looked better in Safari builds with https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/37176 applied (which does _not_ have `menu, dir` in its UA styles). So I suspect this is more due to Chrome/old WebKit considering `li` inside `menu` as standalone `li` and applying quirky behavior there, rather than due to Firefox UA styles covering `menu, dir`.\r\n\r\nI could live either way on including `menu, dir` though, but I'd love to understand the reasoning behind this better.\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/2634494262/reactions",
